&lt;&gt;&lt;</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font color="#0000ff"><font
face="Arial, sans-serif"><font size="4"><strong>THOUGHT PROVOKING &ndash;
INSPIRATIONAL</strong></font></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"> <font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;"><br />
</font></font><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><strong>Would You Ever Deny
Jesus as Peter Did?</strong></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>&quot;Jesus answered, &quot;I tell you,
Peter, before the rooster crows today,</em></font></font></p>
<p align="center" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial,
sans-serif"><font size="2"><em>you will deny three times that you know
me.&quot; Luke 22: 34</em></font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">In the above Scripture, Jesus was telling
Simon Peter he would soon deny that he even knew Him, let alone that he was
a follower, a disciple of&nbsp;His.  Jesus knew that His time was coming.
He knew He was going to be put to death, and He knew that even though Peter
loved Him, and had been at his side, that he would fail the test of
acknowledging His acquaintance.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Peter replied,&nbsp;&quot;Lord, I am
ready to go with you to prison and to death.&quot;  Denying he even knew
Jesus was not something Peter could ever see himself doing; he loved
Jesus.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">We who are Christians wonder how Peter
could possibly renounce the One he claimed to love. We know if it had been
us we could never have done such a thing to Jesus!</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Yet, how many of us deny Jesus even
today?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Do you speak up in a crowd letting those
you are with know that you are a follower of Jesus?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Do you talk of loving God, but never
speak of Jesus?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Do you admit to going to church on Sunday
but join in with Satan's crowd on Monday?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Do you say your prayers before meals at
home, but skip them when you are eating out, not wanting anyone to see
you?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Do you laugh when out in a crowd and
someone tells a dirty joke, instead of showing
disapproval?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">If you knew that you would be put to
death for reading your Bible, or professing to being a Christian, would you
own up to it or would you, too, deny ever having known
Him?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Like Simon Peter we more than likely
could not see ourselves denying Jesus, but most of us have already denied
Him in one way or another at sometime in our lives. Often we fail to speak
up in defense of Jesus, and thus we leave the impression with others that
we are against Him.</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Can you see yourself professing knowing
Jesus, but never see yourself being a Martyr?</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">The day may come when we will be put to
the test. We all need to ask ourselves, &quot;Would I suffer, even give my
life, for the relationship I have with my Lord and Savior, Jesus
Christ?&quot;</font></font></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><br />
</p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="Arial, sans-serif"><font
size="2" style="font-size: 11pt;">Remember Jesus gave His life for you;
would you be willing to do the same for&nbsp; Him?<br />
&nbsp; &nbsp; <br />
